Source: pg-vectorsearch
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-common-dev, postgresql-server-dev-18, gcc (>= 11), make, meson (>= 0.61), ninja-build, python3, pkg-config, libopenblas-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/timescale/pg_vectorsearch

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-vectorsearch
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-vectorsearch
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Approximate nearest neighbor search with PRISM for PostgreSQL PGVERSION
 pg_vectorsearch provides the PRISM index with RaBitQ quantization, SIMD
 distance kernels, and native vec32/vec16 types. It can also index existing
 pgvector vector/halfvec columns without requiring pgvector for standalone
 use. This upstream alpha release is for evaluation.
